<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Henry Harrison</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1773">1773</a>–<a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Henry Harrison was an American soldier and politician, governor of Indiana Territory from 1801 to 1812 and the ninth president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. As governor he pressed land cessions on Native nations, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenskwatawa">Tenskwatawa</a>'s warriors at Tippecanoe in 1811 and beat the British and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumseh">Tecumseh</a> at the Thames in 1813. He died a month after his inauguration in 1841, the first president to die in office.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-henry-harrison.jpg" alt="William Henry Harrison" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albert Gallatin Hoit · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Henry_Harrison_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>President <b>William Henry Harrison</b> died 31 days after taking office, the shortest presidency in US history.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-4">4 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Governor <b>William Henry Harrison</b> of the Indiana Territory marched about 1,000 men against Prophetstown, headquarters of the confederacy of Tecumseh and his brother Tenskwatawa.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-7">7 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Winamac withdrew ahead of reinforcements under <b>William Henry Harrison</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-5">5 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In his absence <b>William Henry Harrison</b> destroyed Prophetstown after the Battle of Tippecanoe in 1811.</blockquote><a href="/state/tecumsehs-confederacy">Tecumseh's Confederacy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Charles City County, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. Died in White House, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=37.35,-77.06&amp;year=1817" aria-label="Charles City County on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2622 819 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of William Henry Harrison"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3072 1089h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3072 1089h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=37.35,-77.06&amp;year=1817">What was here in 1817? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
